Yes, a private buyer can keep cask 214 in the Craigtarry bond. The guidance says private cask owners may keep a cask in the bond for an annual storage and insurance fee, with the distillery holding it under its warehouse approval.

The guidance sets no maximum storage period, so nothing in it prevents a five-year stay. It also doesn't give the fee amount or say whether there are any other terms.

Cask 214 is currently in bond in Warehouse 1 at Craigtarry:
- **Spirit:** Craigtarry single malt
- **Cask type:** refill oloroso sherry butt
- **Filled:** 2 November 2011
- **Strength:** 54.3% ABV
- **Bulk litres:** 431

I can't see the fee or any contract terms, so you would need to confirm those with the distillery directly before purchase.
